  "subtitle": "This month's VMA goes to <i>X-Men</i> #4, where the Angel gets one look at the Scarlet Witch and thinks \"<i>Wow!</i>  What a dish!&nbsp; If <i>she's</i> an evil mutant, I want an application blank!\"\n\n[ASSET: right | PowderingMyNose | width=10%] But we should at least give a shout-out to the Wasp in Avengers 4 ([LINK:1964:AVEN_4|AVEN #4|2027-04-25]), who claims she was off \"powdering her nose\" -- right in the middle of a battle, something she says \"any girl would do in a moment of crisis\"&nbsp; [SPAN: severity=warning; fonttype=bold-italic; text=Yeesh!]",
  "review_text": "Nine graded stories for the month (again <i>Strange Tales</i> providing its normal two)\n\n[SPAN: severity=info; fontsize=large; fonttype=bold; text=x.xx],\n\n... last month's <b>4.31</b>.\n\n\nfor a weighted average of a mere 4.91, which actually surprised me at first since there were four offerings this month that came in at 6.0 or above.&nbsp; But the absolutely <i>dreadful</i> <i>Tales to Astonish</i> continues to drag down everything else, and the Human Torch half of <i>Strange Tales</i> didn't help either.\n\nThe month was highlighted by the appearances of Captain America, the Scarlet Witch and Quicksilver, plus the reappearance of Doc Ock and the battle between the Thing and the Hulk.&nbsp; The Black Widow introduction did not rise to this level of interest, but unbeknownst to the readers of the day, the prominence of this character would of course grow.&nbsp; It certainly <i>felt</i> like a month that delivered good quality, and the influx of new characters (and a very familiar old one) must certainly have been of interest to all.\n\nBut the reality was that the <i>overall</i> quality varied greatly, with the good seeming to be <i>quite</i> solid and the bad really spoiling it for the others.&nbsp; But I walk away from this month mostly satisfied and eagerly look forward to the future offerings!\n\n\n\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** SUMMARY_BEGIN ***\n*** THIS MONTH ***9 graded stories over 8 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 6.33 grade character issue    weight 7.0   aven      AVEN #4  1.00 7.0   asm       ASM #11  1.00 6.0   xmen      XMEN #4  1.00 6.0   ff        FF #25   1.00 4.5   iron      TOS #52  0.50 4.0   thor      JIM #102 0.50 3.5   strange   ST #119  0.33 1.8   giant     TTA #54  0.50 1.5   torch     ST #119  0.505.22*** LAST MONTH ***7 graded stories over 6 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 4.58 grade character issue    weight 9.4   asm       ASM #10  1.00 7.5   thor      JIM #101 0.50 3.0   strange   ST #118  0.33 2.5   giant     TTA #53  0.75 2.5   torch     ST #118  0.50 2.0   iron      TOS #51  0.50 1.5   ff        FF #24   1.004.31\n*** SUMMARY_END ***]",
  "letters_page": "The month was highlighted by the appearances of Captain America, the Scarlet Witch and Quicksilver, plus the reappearance of Doc Ock and the battle between the Thing and the Hulk.&nbsp; The Black Widow introduction also....\n\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** INTRODUCTION_BEGIN ***\nBaron Zemo | villain | unnamed | Milestone: (first)\nHela | villain | Milestone: (first: , in Tales of Asgard)\nLady Sif | Milestone: (first: , in Tales of Asgard)\nNotes | first | villain | Rugga, in Tales of Asgard\nNotes | villain | first | El Toro\nMastermind | villain | Milestone: (first)\nQuicksilver | villain | Milestone: (first), (origin)\nScarlet Witch | villain | Milestone: (first), (origin)\nToad | villain | Milestone: (first)\nNotes | first | villain | Brotherhood of Evil Mutants\nNotes | first | villain | Blackie Gaxton\nNotes | first | death | Bennett Brant\nNotes | first | Spider-Tracer\nNotes | first | villain | Rabble Rouser (Dr. Weinberg)\nNotes | first | villain | Aggamon\nBlack Widow | villain | Milestone: (first)\n*** INTRODUCTION_END ***]\n\n<b>Roundup:</b>\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_BEGIN ***]\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * The Human Torch battles the Rabble Rouser's campaign of mass persuasion, but readers may find themselves fighting to stay interested.\n[HANG0] * Doctor Strange tracks two burglars into the Purple Dimension, confronts its overlord, and wins a mystical beam battle that never quite comes to life.\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_END ***]",
  "ownership": "[HANG0] * We have yet <i>another</i> new character who's a real dare-devil!\n[HANG0] * Thor has to battle a couple of <i>new</i> immortals\n[HANG0] * Giant-Man and the Wasp face the Human Top again\n[HANG0] * The Avengers \"take over\" where the FF left off\n[HANG0] * The Torch runs into Iceman\n[HANG0] * Doctor Strange visits an eerie house\n[HANG0] * Iron Man hasn't heard the last from the Black Widow\n[HANG0] * And Spidey gets unmasked in public!&nbsp; [SPAN: severity=warning; fonttype=bold-italic; text=Oh my!]"
